The calendar is internally exact and agrees with the fixed road table. Day 111 begins at Thornwater and ends above the wash (45:3,41–53); day 112 reaches Lowmarch (45:57; 46:189); day 113 leaves two hours before light, reaches Millrace, takes the fork, and camps at the Stair (47:3,21–33,239–245; 48:129–279); day 114 contains the trap, stalemate, ascent and night recovery (49:3; 51:197); day 115 contains the perimeter and kit recovery (52:3–59,355–359). This continues directly from Oryn leaving on day 111 and reaching the mill water near dusk on day 112 (44:225–247,297–305).

Oryn's lateness arithmetic is also consistent: due Millrace day 96, present day 112 gives sixteen; the oxen ford on day 121 against day 104 gives seventeen, plus the two-day detour gives nineteen; the child moves to no earlier than day 128 (47:133–155). No arrival or road-time count contradicts `STATE_LEDGER.md:55`.

The Millrace exception is stated plainly without comment on her earlier word “north”: the water from north and east meets the circuit road and brings her to Millrace (47:9–15), after the earlier carter reports that she came down the mill water from the hill track (45:71–79). The old woman's knee planted in Oryn's day-111 sum arrives at her table (44:245–253; 47:61–81).

