+## (4) Reader clarity
+
+Speaker attribution and action geography pass throughout. The contract council, Millrace line, Stair crossing, underground stalemate, declaration, treatment, two-visit kit reading and wall research all retain clear owners and referents. The action explains each operational rule before it is needed, and the Reader Standard gates are clean.
+
+For a fluent thirteen-year-old, two points do not yet survive a first reading:
+
+- In chapters 47–48 the text currently says Cael asks to read Oryn at the bench and then asks to read Oryn on the road, while protected dialogue insists it is “a different question.” Location and fatigue do not make those questions different enough, and the source says something else. Fixes 1–6 keep the wrist patient present, make the refusal about touching that patient during treatment, and make the grant about reading the consenting teacher.
+- In chapter 52, 220 yards cannot be literal spacing along a ten-stride chamber wall. Fix 7 identifies a scaled interval inside the incised line before the protected number is spoken. It clarifies the observable method only; it supplies no decoding or theory.
+
