   old: `He stood for as long as it took him to be sure that he had nothing to add, and he had nothing. He had asked a person for the first time in his life whether he might do a thing to her; she had said that he might not; and the whole of what was left to him was to go and sit down. He went and sat down. It was not hard to do, and he was a little surprised at that, since he had dreaded it.`
   new: `He stood for as long as it took him to be sure that he had nothing to add, and he had nothing. For the first time in his life, he had asked before putting his hand on another person; he had been told that he might not; and the whole of what was left to him was to go and sit down. He went and sat down. It was not hard to do, and he was a little surprised at that, since he had dreaded it.`

