+## (2) Continuity
+
+### Counts, calendar and capabilities
+
+- The movement runs from the 111th through the 115th day and joins cleanly from chapter 44's dawn on the 111th into Movement 8's post-Stair entry state.
+- Deployment rises from thirteen to **fourteen** with Tide on Oryn, then the nine lines in the night log—Anchor look at the stakes; Shadow; the read; Anchor look for the knot; Anchor unbinding; Wind; Storm; Compression; Ember—bring the sum to **twenty-three** (`chapter-51.md:193–217`). The log and chapter 52's closing entry agree.
+- Shadow occurs once in this movement and for the second time in the book. The on-page seal is complete: Cael is below the floor, Lira is on the thirty-fourth step, Seln has his back turned, Brom/Oryn/Karis are beyond the doorway's corner, and the faceless rim is 260 yards away without a sightline below the lip. Oryn is not told Shadow's source. What the rim and Teague see is only a practitioner emerge and declare outside; Teague asks nothing.
+- The rim remains six faceless people with no name, seal or office. Teague's crew remains unnamed. Oryn is a stop on her route, never a sixth member and never joined.
+- The Stair's three hundred is taken and never paid. The case is untouched. The index and stroke-and-bar remain undecoded; no maker, sender, purpose or causal theory is supplied.
+
+### The three coordinator questions
+
+1. **Chapter 52 radius spacing — AMEND.** The full source unit does not explain the number as a scale, an encoded figure or a sheet interval. Read literally, it says Karis “paced the spacing” of a line recurring on the chamber walls at 220 yards and a stride; that cannot fit a chamber ten strides across. Current `chapter-52.md:251` reinforces the literal reading by making her walk the wall with a cord while “counting.” The protected unit cannot be changed. Line fix 7 therefore establishes outside it that she is reading scaled divisions **within** the lone line, not measuring distance along the wall. That makes the protected figure intelligible without decoding what the line means or why it is there.
+2. **Oryn's “different question” — AMEND.** The author's location/role reading is not the source's full distinction. At the lean-to, Cael asks permission to touch **the boy's wrist while Oryn works**, in order to feel what she feels; Oryn refuses because the patient did not come to be practised on. On the road, Cael asks to read **Oryn herself**; she is the person under his hand and can consent, and the reading is now a deliberate lesson (surface, then a minute of the long reading). Bench versus rock and tired versus rested are circumstances, not the governing difference. Current chapters 47–48 instead make both requests “may I read you,” contradicting the protected line; the current chapter 47 has also dismissed every patient before the request. Fixes 1–6 leave the last small patient waiting with a wrist injury and restore the different patient, consenter and purpose in fresh wording without changing protected text or creating an unprotected source quotation.
+3. **Roof height — PASS.** Chapter 49 presents Cael's rushed estimate: he “judged it a foot above Brom's head” (`chapter-49.md:193`). On the 115th he re-paces the room; Brom touches the roof with a bent elbow and says, “A hand … I wasn't standing up straight” (`chapter-52.md:87–91`). “None of them had been” explicitly makes it a correction under pressure, not a retcon. It agrees with the forty-step stair and does not conflict with Movement 8's separate twelve-stride, roofless Hall.
+
+### Knowledge boundaries, protected defaults and handoff
+
+The debt remains owed: one self-reading has been done; Oryn refuses a hurried second; two readings on different days and the whole telling remain due, on her day. Nothing is forgiven. “The still place” is absent. “Tomorrow makes three” is not repeated or explained. The #50 council line remains verbatim and unglossed; the case's twelve years occurs only in Seln's separate window. “Compact” is not said in the movement.
+
+The chapter 52 chamber now has no manuscript trace of a continuous groove. The forty-one kinds are explicitly “in the courses”; the protected lone line is between them; the design is confirmed once; and the dated old irons are separated from the later, undated mark. Those facts agree with the binding Movement 7 ledger ruling and the Movement 8 packet.
+
+One closeout record needs refresh, not a manuscript repair: the lower, pre-repair “New canon minted (author's list)” in `STATE_LEDGER.md` still says the roof is a foot above Brom and describes a level groove. The controlling coordinator rulings immediately above it and the current prose correctly say a hand and no groove. The coordinator should replace those stale author-list sentences when closing the movement.
