+# CLOSE WITH LINE FIXES — seven local replacements
+
+Scope: six local paragraphs in chapters 47–48 must keep the final wrist patient at the bench and restore the source's actual distinction between the refused lean-to request and the granted road request; one chapter 52 sentence must establish that the protected radius figure is read from scaled divisions within the lone line, not as literal spacing along a ten-stride wall. No protected unit is altered, no scene rewrite or second repair is needed, and the settled length is not reopened.
+
+## (1) Brief items
+
+Baseline for every repair quotation below: `state/movement-007/pre-repair-r1/`, the frozen draft after the coordinator's ten plan-audit fixes, compared with `diff -U0` against the current manuscript. I read the full current movement before making these rulings.
+
+### A. Three tracked passages in chapter 52 — RESOLVED
+
+1. **The stair's air — RESOLVED.** The baseline chain began, “At the twentieth the air changed … both flames stood up straight and still,” then immediately supplied the cold and the missing smells. The repair enters on the bolt at the thirty-first step (`chapter-52.md:61–65`); Brom notices the wrong flame first—“It's stood like that since a good way back. Like a nail”—and only afterward does Seln locate the change: “Since the twentieth … The air stops there” (`52:69–79`). Oryn supplies the cold and absent earth/water smells after all six enter the chamber (`52:81–85`). The source's same-content/same-order chain is broken.
+2. **The “proper catalogue” — RESOLVED.** The diff deletes “Cael catalogued the room properly, since nobody had been able to the day before.” The repaired scene begins the chamber work with an actual check: “Cael paced the room from the door to the western wall, and then across” (`52:87`). The present measurement corrects yesterday's rushed roof estimate before the narration explains why all of them had misjudged it (`52:87–93`). The source frame—announced proper catalogue followed by a comparison with yesterday—is gone.
+3. **The open kit — RESOLVED.** The baseline opened, “It was a case … The lid stood open and thrown right back,” then moved to contents, taking-out order and interrupted work. The repair begins on the half-run cord—“It was the cord that Cael's eye went along first”—then lets Brom name the tools and Karis state their functions (`52:127–133`). The open case is identified only afterward (`52:135`), and Seln reads the taking-out order last (`52:137`). The required facts remain in a new order.
+
+I reopened source chapter 20 for all three passages named in `source-tracking.md` and applied the same-content/same-order standard rather than relying on the automatic percentage. All three returned passages are **RESOLVED**. **New tracking: none.** The repaired roof correction, two-visit dating, and wall-work support do not reproduce a new source chain. The overlap command independently reports zero unprotected shared runs of eight or more words.
+
+### B. Confirm the design once — RESOLVED
+
+The perimeter supplies the single size/design confirmation. The diff compresses the baseline's repeated “The same size … The both of them” / “To a stride … the same size twice” into “Then they're the one size” and Karis's one answer, “To a stride” (`chapter-52.md:53–57`). Later work produces new findings rather than re-proving the same proposition: forty-one kinds **in the courses** (`52:283–289`), then the separate line **between** the courses (`52:291–301`). The closing log no longer repeats “Karis has the round, and it is the Fallow's.” The one remaining clarity defect is not repeated proof but the impossible literal sound of the protected spacing number; line fix 7 resolves that without touching the protected unit.
+
+### C. The set piece told once — RESOLVED
+
+The repair removes **891 words** across chapters 49–51 (5,146 → 4,885; 5,669 → 5,324; 6,829 → 6,544) while preserving every exchange, rule, fragment use and bill. Representative `diff -U0` evidence:
+
